{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization is safely applicable to this workflow. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (cache dependency downloads) is already satisfied: the workflow configures `cache: pnpm` in the setup-node step and runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, so an equivalent dependency cache already exists and the pattern's contraindication applies. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT (bound jobs with a custom timeout) is the only other workflow_yaml-scoped candidate, but its precondition requires representative successful-duration history, and the repository reports no completed CI runs; without history a safe timeout cannot be determined and the contraindication that valid slow runs could exceed the limit cannot be ruled out. All remaining patterns are inapplicable: there is no matrix (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST), no test suite to prioritize/select (P-LIT-PRIORITIZE, P-LIT-SELECT), no Bazel build (P-LIT-BAZEL-*), and the rest are ci_service-scoped rather than workflow-file changes.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT"]
}
